DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't chase Nvidia's pop or Anthropic's debut.</b> Nvidia beat and guided to $130B, rising ~3-4% after hours, but earnings-night moves can fade at the open; Anthropic prices Wednesday (US) and trades Thursday, and day-one IPO swings can be big. A broad index fund already gives you AI exposure.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Fear & Greed is 25 (edge of Extreme Fear) and 420 NYSE stocks hit new lows vs 18 highs — the weakest breadth in our chart. Fixed monthly buys (DCA) beat guessing the bottom.",
"<b>Plan for more rate hikes.</b> A December quarter-point hike is ~93-95% priced and the St. Louis Fed's Musalem talked of up to four; lock fixed rates where you can and avoid adding variable-rate debt.",
"<b>Cash and short bonds still pay you to wait.</b> With the 2Y near 4.81% and hikes coming, keep your emergency fund and near-term money in high-yield savings or short-term bonds.",
"<b>Don't buy the dip in one chip stock.</b> Even after a strong report, Nvidia is down sharply this month amid a CEO fight and China rules; if you want chips, spread it across a fund and keep it small.",
"<b>Fuel relief is holding, mostly.</b> US diesel is ~$5.98 and Brent is ~20% lower this month, but US-Iran strikes and tanker attacks keep prices jumpy — budget for swings.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a rocket.</b> At ~$3,851 it is near a one-year low as rates rise; hold a small slice for protection rather than chasing it.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC ~$64.9k is stuck near three-month lows; only invest what you can afford to see fall a lot more.",
"<b>Thai investors: tech-led dip, rotate gently.</b> The SET fell 1.66% to 1,474.68 on DELTA's slide and foreigners sold ฿997M; brokers see 1,455-1,495 Wednesday. Steady dividend payers and non-tech large caps can cushion a choppy market.",
"<b>War headlines swing both ways.</b> The US struck an Iranian missile site yet oil rose under 1% — avoid panic-selling on headlines and keep a diversified mix."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 25 = the line between Fear and Extreme Fear, down from 31 Monday and 37 a week ago, but above 18 a month ago. Momentum, put/call, VIX and safe-haven demand read extreme fear; junk bonds are neutral."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~48 = Elevated (up from 46.4): a direct US strike on Iran's Qeshm Island and new bridge strikes in Ukraine nudged factors up; Thursday's Trump-Xi-Putin summit stays on track."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 5.2 = extreme fear, down from 9.2 as the S&P hit its lowest close since July."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 36.6 = fear, down from 41.4 as NYSE new lows reached 420."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 44.6 = fear, down from a neutral 49.4."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 15.0 = extreme fear, from 19.6: traders kept buying protection into Nvidia's report."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. 17.8 on CNN's 0-100 scale = extreme fear, down from 33.3 as volatility rose."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 7.2 = extreme fear, down from 11.8: Treasuries rallied while stocks fell."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 50.0 = neutral, down from 52.4; junk bonds yield near 8%."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 66 (from 63): US warplanes struck an Iranian missile site on Qeshm Island after drones targeted a US radar in Bahrain."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 40 (from 38): Russia hit Kyiv's bridges and Ukraine hit the Kerch bridge; Berlin talks are planned but Moscow resists Europe's role."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 87 (from 86): more claimed Hormuz mine hits and Houthi claims of strikes on Saudi pipeline pumps."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 10 (steady): Thursday's three-way summit is on track and Qatar keeps mediating with Iran."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 32 (steady): nuclear-arms reduction is expected at Thursday's summit; Iran still bars IAEA inspections of damaged sites."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,341 Tuesday (−1.03%), its lowest close since late July and a fourth straight loss."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −1.64% Tuesday (−849 pts) to about 50,759."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −0.74% Tuesday to about 24,328 after touching its lowest since April intraday; Nvidia's beat lifted futures after the close."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~5.10% Tuesday, down 2bp for a second day after Friday's 5.17%."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$86.0 (+0.3%) Tuesday as Gulf attacks offset surplus forecasts."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$93.1 at Tuesday's settle (+0.8%), still ~20% lower this month."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$5.98/gal (AAA, 17 Nov), a second day under $6."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,851 spot Tuesday (−0.2%), near a one-year low; rising rates and a strong dollar keep it under pressure."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$64.9k = still bearish: flat early Wednesday after a ~2% dip Tuesday; it trades with tech, not as a haven."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% after September's hike, held 28 Oct; a December hike is ~93-95% priced for 8-9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. October rose 0.4% MoM (est. 0.3%) and core 0.3% (est. 0.2%), a third straight upside surprise; no official YoY because of last year's data gap, well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. October rose 0.3% MoM (est. 0.4%) and 6.5% YoY, the highest since November 2022; core +0.3%."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). ~93-95% for a quarter point in December; ~68% for another in January."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. It touched a fresh 19-month high Tuesday before easing."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~159.4, just under the 160 level where Japan has warned about intervention."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) in October; its bonds now yield ~15% (CNBC, 17 Nov)."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct (unanimous). Minutes say policy should stay accommodative; the BoT is now prioritising new SME credit tools for 2027; next decision 23 Dec."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,474.68 Tue 17 Nov (−1.66%) as DELTA fell ฿8; brokers see 1,455-1,495 Wednesday."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. −฿996.79M of Thai stocks on Tue 17 Nov, after +฿1,200M Monday."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};

